#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068542 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068681 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "62bb3b79-407f-511b-913d-f47b3ea6d822" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Circumference of a Circle Given the Diameter"}] :question/id #uuid "ba3d3abd-4b93-5705-8fcb-cb88b58dad2f" :question/math-academy-id "e-3178" :question/problem "What is the circumference $C$ of a circle with a diameter of $d=10?$ \n\n![](images/b1/b1ebd81fca9688b5688dc916d6be62bad14853f55a8e66c5c7af469dd4032ec4.png)" :question/worked-solution "We use the formula $C=\\pi d$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =\\pi d \\\\  & =\\pi \\cdot 10 \\\\  & =10\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the exact answer. If we want an approximate answer, say rounded to three decimal places, we can use the approximation $\\pi\\approx 3.14\\,159,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =10\\cdot \\pi  \\\\  & ≈10\\cdot 3.14\\,159 \\\\  & ≈31.416.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068543 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068682 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "27538979-a350-50d2-9c55-cebf0bd7e78b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Circumference of a Circle Given the Radius"}] :question/id #uuid "d26dfc25-605c-5d73-80bc-15801b20beb5" :question/math-academy-id "e-3179" :question/problem "What is the circumference $C$ of a circle with a radius of $6?$\n\n![](images/3c/3c21021529285f488ca794a442e5826a033ed2a4c6f4fad53ab9e8fdc84d35ee.png)" :question/worked-solution "We use the formula $C=2\\pi r$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =2\\pi r \\\\  & =2\\pi \\cdot 6 \\\\  & =12\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068544 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068683 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "09b24ba2-e9c9-5839-81df-09720bc9c7d8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Radius or Diameter of a Circle Given the Circumference"}] :question/id #uuid "af77eddf-8816-5b03-a53d-0f29f1f1a1b3" :question/math-academy-id "e-3180" :question/problem "What is the radius $r$ of a circle with a circumference of $C=17\\pi?$\n\n![](images/69/697cc9ca06bcfe46d84dfab74e0f6ae83f4342607ea4af138b111606c16e8a03.png)" :question/worked-solution "We use the formula for the circumference $C=2\\pi r$ and solve for $r.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =2\\pi r \\\\ 17\\pi  & =2\\pi r \\\\ r & =\\frac{17\\pi }{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{2} \\\\  & =8.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068545 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068684 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "89403c66-caac-5f6b-bacd-9f2a74525198" :knowledge-point/title "Word Problems"}] :question/id #uuid "e18e4cc8-8ecb-53e9-8b12-c9cb5b926aa7" :question/math-academy-id "e-3182" :question/problem "Carol has to wrap a rope around a circular column whose diameter is $20\\,\\textrm{cm}.$ What length of the rope will wrap the column perfectly?" :question/worked-solution "The length of the rope needed to wrap around the column is its circumference.\n\nThe formula for the circumference of a circle is $C = \\pi d$, where $d=20\\,\\textrm{cm}$ is the diameter. \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nC = \\pi\\cdot 20 = 20\\pi \\,\\textrm{cm}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497391 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068681 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "62bb3b79-407f-511b-913d-f47b3ea6d822" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Circumference of a Circle Given the Diameter"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3298fbad-dfc7-588e-b38c-20a57b427c71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{yd}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496767} {:answer/id #uuid "b043737b-735c-537e-a961-a9037a95c0a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi \\,\\text{yd}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497015} {:answer/id #uuid "c18793f8-6949-5175-b11f-dd92927bff74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 1759218604549