e formula for the circumference $C=2\\pi r$ and solve for $r.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =2\\pi r \\\\ 7 & =2\\pi r \\\\ r & =\\frac{7}{2\\pi }\\,\\text{m}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497399 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068683 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "09b24ba2-e9c9-5839-81df-09720bc9c7d8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Radius or Diameter of a Circle Given the Circumference"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08702ecd-ba2a-5dc4-a61b-587184515899" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496673} {:answer/id #uuid "10c4a483-8085-5d16-911c-be7f848c5f52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496693} {:answer/id #uuid "45d9e406-7f39-5af9-87d1-244fdbdd4f03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496808} {:answer/id #uuid "5cf1406c-bfb3-5204-94bb-dfbf812784ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496862} {:answer/id #uuid "9f31ae9f-7d96-5240-9377-5f2c2a8bd26c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496989}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5cf1406c-bfb3-5204-94bb-dfbf812784ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496862} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f9626a0-67b1-590b-90d1-2f7438f67929" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497261}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c2fe80a7-5526-5b19-979f-2b18ba9fc425" :question/math-academy-id "q-122032" :question/problem "![](images/e0/e046aafb09255a579c76a48f0f422627761a19451ae36a053424a8ac8a3332f7.png)\n\nWhat is the diameter of a circle with a circumference of $\\frac{5\\pi }{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "We use the formula for the circumference $C=\\pi d$ and solve for $d.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =\\pi d \\\\ \\frac{5\\pi }{2} & =\\pi d \\\\ d & =\\frac{5\\pi }{2\\pi } \\\\ d & =\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497338 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068683 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "09b24ba2-e9c9-5839-81df-09720bc9c7d8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Radius or Diameter of a Circle Given the Circumference"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12d8fbfd-f3db-53ff-b98a-0cff0ed19456" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9\\,\\text{ft}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496699} {:answer/id #uuid "5c369159-c893-5584-a4e8-d9c17c11c023" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\pi \\,\\text{ft}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496860} {:answer/id #uuid "a01f82a3-a3b2-562a-a714-110588418699" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\,\\text{ft}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496992} {:answer/id #uuid "a5a03208-6893-5823-b472-bde68ebd603b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,\\text{ft}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497000} {:answer/id #uuid "cc26f2a6-15ea-5a56-b9c2-d373483bcbe0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\,\\text{ft}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497079}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc26f2a6-15ea-5a56-b9c2-d373483bcbe0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\,\\text{ft}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497079} :answer-field/id #uuid "975c17ad-d8c3-5189-bedc-fac0a72dbaf4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497289}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1d3f49ce-877b-5ae1-8337-866d03e886d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-3735" :question/problem "![](images/57/5782df9eb0a0055ef071647a133bf6cadf7c5121a160a4ffe2383efa899535e0.png)\n\nWhat is the diameter of a circle with a circumference of $12\\pi \\,\\text{ft}?$" :question/worked-solution "We use the formula for the circumference $C=\\pi d$ and solve for $d.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =\\pi d \\\\ 12\\pi  & =\\pi d \\\\ d & =\\frac{12\\pi }{\\pi } \\\\ d & =12\\,\\text{ft}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069430 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068684 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "89403c66-caac-5f6b-bacd-9f2a74525198" :knowledge-point/title "Word Problems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95a2dad9-0547-53b2-b54b-36b4192e877d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30\\pi \\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496969} {:answer/id #uuid "96ace683-1432-5b37-90f5-77548e014d86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi \\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496972} {:answer/id #uuid "d1913280-fe19-5501-8536-b0d76434a0a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497095} {:answer/id #uuid "e48372d3-e37a-5407-a1ff-e01f1204dac3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60\\pi \\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497147} {:answer/id #uuid "f59a7da9-9cf4-567a-b2b9-156ace337242" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15\\pi \\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497182}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "95a2dad9-0547-53b2-b54b-36b4192e877d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30\\pi \\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496969} :answer-field/id #uuid "6cc22b08-f4a6-5ada-8fe7-444636f12ecd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067750}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "21f64099-6f70-52f4-bd49-e0e0761a9208" :question/math-academy-id "q-53553" :question/problem "![](images/ad/ad42b4bd62bf64e1ac086a60ace286b3e6d1c136f423d2ae6aabf6339cea9071.png)\n\nWhat length of fence is needed to border a circular plot of land with a diameter of $30\\,\\text{m}?$" :question/worked-solution "The length of the fence needed to border the circular land is its circumference.\n\nThe formula for the circumference of a circle is $C=\\pi d,$ where $d=30\\,\\text{m}$ is the diameter.\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nC=\\pi \\cdot 30=30\\pi \\,\\text{m}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497327 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068684 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "89403c66-caac-5f6b-bacd-9f2a74525198" :knowledge-point/title "Word Problems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7a2abbe0-b911-5ed0-b8cb-f6c69ce3381b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\pi \\,\\text{yd}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496914} {:answer/id #uuid "983e66cd-9dd5-5e32-86f0-ba0838837e94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi \\,\\text{yd}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496977} {:answer/id #uuid "ac14585a-95cc-5525-b26d-ec79bfbcf958" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,\\text{yd}" :db/id #edb/ref 17